  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2021_W30_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-30",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2021_W30_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-30.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2021-07-30",
  "report_week": "30",
  "report_period": "Week 30 (23rd Jul to 30th Jul 2021)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Japanese owners committed their Post Panamax \"Harvest Sky\" 95/2013 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 23 mill basis delivery October 2021, Meanwhile, the \"Dyna Camellia\" 91/2007 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 03/2022, BWTS fitted) from Hsin Chien Marine was sold to Chinese buyers for USD 17,5 mill basis delivery September-October 2021. Marubeni Corp sold their Kamsarmax \"Glorious Wind\" 83/2010 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 08/2025, DD 09/2023) to Greek buyers for excess USD 20 mill basis delivery November-December 2021. Note that the one-year-younger \"Magnolia\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 11/2025, DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 22 mill basis delivery February 2022. On the Ultramax sector, the \"Komi\" 63/2015 Cosco Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2025, DD 03/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold to Greek buyers for USD 25 mill basis delivery September 2021 with T/C attached until November of 2021. Moreover, Big Fame Shipping sold their \"Ocean Phoenix Tree\" 62/2017 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 09/2022, BWTS fitted) for USD 29,5 mill basis delivery January 2022. In addition, Archangel Pacific sold their \"Calico Jack\" 61/2015 I-S, Japan (SS 10/2025, DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) & \"Phoenix Rising\" 60/2015 Mitsui, Japan (SS 06/2025, DD 06/2023, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 55 mill enbloc including balance of T/C. AM Nomikos sold their Supramax \"Dory\" 55/2010 IHI, Japan (SS 09/2025, DD 04/2024, BWTS & Grabs fitted) for USD 17,5 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older \"Nord Trust\" 55/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 10/2024, DD 10/2022) was sold a week ago at USD 16 mill. The Handysize \"Ms Charm\" 32/2010 Zhejiang, China (SS 07/2025, DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold to undisclosed buyers for USD 12,5 mill. For comparison, the \"Ming Yuan\" 33/2010 Taizhou, China (SS 07/2025, DD 08/2023) was sold earlier this month at USD 11 mill.",
    "tankers": "NYK Line have committed their VLCC \"Tsuruga\" 310/2009 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2024, DD 10/2022) to Greek buyers for USD 39 mill. Note that the Korean built \"Athenian Victory\" 317/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS 09/2024, DD 08/2022) was sold back in June at USD 42,5 mill. Sovcomflot sold their Suezmax sister vessels \"Scf Ural\" & \"Scf Caucasus\" 159/2002 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 07/2022 & 03/2022 respectively) to Far Eastern buyers for USD 16,4 mill each. Remind you that the \"Vladimir Velikiy\" 160/2002 Samho, Korea (SS/DD 01/2022) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 16,2 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 13,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 28,000/29,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 28,000/29,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into China with iron ore were fixed around usd 31,000/32,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via West Africa with bauxite were fixed around usd 30,000/31,500 pd. Continental trips into China were reported at the level of usd 49,000/49,500 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips via Black Sea were fixed around usd 33,000/35,000 pd. On the period front a Kamsarmax were reported fixed in the usd 31,000 pd for 3/5 months employment basis delivery in the Pacific.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A generally quiet week for this segment with limited fresh information. A number of Chinese trips into Philippines with steels were reported fixed in the usd 25,000/26,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 41,000/42,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 30,000/31,000 pd. Continental trips via Baltic into Mediterranean with timber were reported at the level of usd 22,000/23,000 pd. US Gulf trips via Mississippi River into West Coast Central America were fixed around usd 35,000/36,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
